WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:03.430
The janitor was holding a push broom.

2
00:00:03.431 --> 00:00:07.306
He looked confused as he came toward them.

3
00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:10.347
"Where are the bugs I'm supposed to sweep away?"

4
00:00:10.348 --> 00:00:13.403
Mr. Neal hurried out of the building.

5
00:00:13.404 --> 00:00:15.651
"It's strange, Mr. Patel.

6
00:00:15.652 --> 00:00:18.216
I don't hear the crickets anymore.

7
00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:21.619
It's as if they all just disappeared."

8
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.630
The janitor shrugged.

9
00:00:23.631 --> 00:00:25.945
"Maybe they left on their own."

10
00:00:25.946 --> 00:00:28.154
"Some did, but . . ."

11
00:00:28.155 --> 00:00:31.448
Mr. Neal ran a hand through his hair.

12
00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:33.825
"But there were so many of them.

13
00:00:33.826 --> 00:00:37.042
Oh well, sorry to bother you.

14
00:00:37.043 --> 00:00:41.718
I'll call you if they come back."

15
00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:52.611
After the janitor left, Mr. Neal brought the class back inside.

16
00:00:52.612 --> 00:01:03.740
As they entered the classroom, everyone passed the empty, tipped-over tank.

17
00:01:03.741 --> 00:01:09.823
"So much for our class pets," Raj said with a sigh.

18
00:01:09.824 --> 00:01:14.339
"It's all Daisy's fault." Parker pointed at Daisy.

19
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.182
"She's the one who set the crickets free."

20
00:01:18.183 --> 00:01:24.177
"I already told you, Parker. I didn't do it," Daisy said.

21
00:01:24.178 --> 00:01:28.226
"Well, I think you did."

22
00:01:28.227 --> 00:01:30.759
Parker flopped into his seat.

23
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:36.656
"I saw you sneak into the school when we were supposed to stay outside."

24
00:01:36.657 --> 00:01:41.229
"That was after the crickets got out, you dummy," Kaleem said.

25
00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:45.797
"And she was using the restroom."

26
00:01:45.798 --> 00:01:50.961
"No name calling allowed in this classroom," Mr. Neal said sternly.

27
00:01:50.962 --> 00:01:54.847
"Take your seats, please."

28
00:01:54.848 --> 00:02:00.388
The students sat at their desks, still talking about the cricket incident.

29
00:02:00.389 --> 00:02:03.700
"Sorry for the name calling," Kaleem said.

30
00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:07.524
"But, Parker, you're lying about Daisy."

31
00:02:07.525 --> 00:02:12.779
"No, I'm not," Parker said. "I saw her sneak into the building.

32
00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.629
I bet she stomped those crickets herself to hide the evidence of her crime."

33
00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:19.599
Kaleem rolled his eyes.

34
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.580
"Crime? The tank tipped over. That's it, Parker."

35
00:02:24.581 --> 00:02:29.959
Parker scowled. "Maybe you helped Daisy do it, Kaleem."

36
00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:33.662
"Daisy didn't do it," Grace said bravely.

37
00:02:33.663 --> 00:02:38.319
When everyone turned to stare at her, her cheeks turned pink.

38
00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:43.507
"I told you, I was with her for the whole recess period."

39
00:02:43.508 --> 00:02:46.157
"That's good enough for me."

40
00:02:46.158 --> 00:02:51.415
Mr. Neal was busy setting the tank right-side up and tidying the counter.

41
00:02:51.416 --> 00:02:54.396
"Grace always tells the truth."

42
00:02:54.397 --> 00:02:58.997
"Besides, everyone knows Daisy loves animals," Kaleem said.

43
00:02:58.998 --> 00:03:01.759
"She wouldn't hurt insects."

44
00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.844
"So how did the crickets escape?" Raj asked.

45
00:03:05.845 --> 00:03:13.822
Parker smirked. "Maybe Daisy talked to them and convinced them to leave on their own."

46
00:03:13.823 --> 00:03:19.231
Daisy froze. She was so surprised that she couldn't speak for a moment.

47
00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:22.038
Had Parker guessed her secret?

48
00:03:22.039 --> 00:03:28.204
"Oh, I could almost believe that," Grace said, her eyes going wide.

49
00:03:28.205 --> 00:03:33.818
"I mean Daisy does seem to be talking to animals sometimes.

50
00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:41.575
I heard her talking to my fish, and then there's this dog next door named Scamp . . ."

51
00:03:41.576 --> 00:03:43.732
Her voice trailed off.

52
00:03:43.733 --> 00:03:51.159
Raj laughed. "Maybe Daisy is like the guy in that book we read in class.

53
00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.432
What was his name again?"

54
00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:57.249
"Doctor Dolittle!" several kids called out.

55
00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:01.291
"Hey, Daisy, do you only speak cricket?" Parker asked.

56
00:04:01.292 --> 00:04:07.697
"Or can you talk to all animals, like Doctor Dolittle?"

57
00:04:07.698 --> 00:04:12.970
Suddenly everyone was staring at Daisy, including Mr. Neal.

58
00:04:12.971 --> 00:04:15.004
Daisy looked away.

59
00:04:15.005 --> 00:04:20.838
Her eyes landed on the window, where Beatrice was buzzing around nervously.

60
00:04:20.839 --> 00:04:23.261
"Uh-oh," Daisy thought.

61
00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:29.950
"I think I messed up—big-time!"

